Homepage: https://github.com/hugomonizdorego/Eduka-Lafa
Description: Lafa - encyclopedia of Timor-Leste and virtual assistant
 Lafa Desktop is an interactive encyclopedia of Timor-Leste, from the
 formation of the island and its fossils to 2026: prehistory, history,
 colonial times and the occupation, the State, its institutions and
 leaders, the Constitution of the RDTL (full text in Tetun and
 Portuguese with fast search), the national symbols with the anthem
 "Patria" and lyrics that follow the music, culture, sports, society,
 economy, land and nature, the 14 municipalities on an interactive map,
 tourist places, public holidays, a "millionaire" quiz, more than 1000
 Tetun words with their meaning in Portuguese, Indonesian, English and
 other ASEAN and CPLP languages, and learning paths for the school
 levels of the Ministry of Education. The interface and the texts are in
 Tetun and Portuguese, the official languages, with sources and licences.
 .
 Everything works offline. With internet, Lafa can download Wikipedia
 introductions and free-licence photos for offline use, World Bank data
 and new content (checked with SHA-256). No login, no AI, no server.
 .
 The optional Lafa Virtual Assistant (switched on in Eduka-Settings ->
 Lafa-Configuration) is a Timor-Leste guide and study buddy on the
 Eduka-Panel: daily facts, holidays, Tetun words and mini quizzes.
